@ Index:  Tests that x≈? follows display FIX
@ Author: Rémy Trotin
@ Tested: XEQ ‘TSTAEQ’
@ Input:  none; runs its four built-in pairs
@ Output: All four return PASSED
@
@ TSTAEQ tries four pairs: a real against a long integer, a real against
@ a complex, a real against a real, and a complex against a complex.
@
@ Helper subroutine A compares Y and X: agreement at FIX 03 is a failure,
@ and agreement only at FIX 02 is a pass.
LBL A
  FIX 03
  𝑥≈? Y             ; equal at 3 decimals is too close
    GTO 01
  FIX 02
  𝑥≈? Y             ; equal at 2 decimals is the expected pass
    GTO 02

  LBL 01
    NDROP 02
    ‘FAILED’
    GTO 03

  LBL 02
    NDROP 02
    ‘PASSED’

    LBL 03
      STOP
      NDROP 02
      RTN

    LBL ‘TSTAEQ’
      ‘R34-LI’      ; real against a long integer
      1.001
      1
      XEQ A
      ‘R34-CPX’     ; real against a complex
      1.001
      1.002+0.𝒾
      XEQ A
      ‘R34-R34’     ; real against a real
      1.001
      1.002
      XEQ A
      ‘CPX-CPX’     ; complex against a complex
      1.001+1.002𝒾
      1.003+1.004𝒾
      XEQ A
  END
.END.
